  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rights and Justice Activity (RAJA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Uganda):  The purpose of the Rights and Justice Activity (RAJA) is to increase citizens&apos; ability to exercise their rights and enjoy their fundamental freedoms in a safe and secure manner, and ensure that victims of human rights abuses have access to justice, protection, and referral services. This activity will focus on advancing three objectives:.Objective 1 - Advocacy: Individuals and organizations defend and maintain the legislative frameworks that enable civic and political activism and ensure access to justice, particularly for children..Objective 2 - Physical Security, Digital Security, and Compliance Support: Individuals and organizations exercising civil and political rights do so more safely and securely in the face of physical, digital, and legal threats..Objective 3 - Legal Aid and Social Services for Victims: Vulnerable populations such as human rights defenders, women, children, youth, LGBTI, and people with disabilities whose rights are violated can access legal remedies and social services...</narrative>
  </description>
